    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d531">

                <pb facs="0699" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg575"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2033: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-04-12T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12,
                                1921—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received April 12—3:16
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>152. Your telegram no. 18, January 20.<anchor n="91" xml:id="d531-f1"/> A nearly
                    verbatim copy of the text of that cable has been received by the British
                    Legation which has been instructed to cable its views after consulting this
                    Legation on the matter.</p>
                <p>It is the desire of the British Legation to learn what governments, besides that
                    of Great Britain, the American Government has approached. I desire instructions
                    as to the extent I have authority to discuss this proposal and with whom.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d531-f1" n="91" xml:id="d531-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; no. 18 was sent to the Chargé in Japan with instructions to repeat
                    to the Minister in China as no. 33. See footnote 76, <ref target="#pg564">p.
                        564</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
